<urn:atm:triage:finding/FTQ-027>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FTQ-027" ;
  triage:title "std::sync::Barrier::wait() with no timeout in singleton recovery test — spawned thread panic causes permanent test hang (tests.rs:342)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/tests.rs:342 — singleton_guard_rejects_stale_recovery_when_owner_token_changes uses std::sync::Barrier::new(2) for rendezvous coordination. The spawned thread (line 341) calls HostOwnershipAdapter::acquire_at which performs file I/O and lock acquisition. If that thread panics before reaching its own barrier.wait() call, the Barrier internal count is never satisfied and the test thread blocks at line 342 indefinitely. std::sync::Barrier has no timeout API and does not propagate thread panics, so a panic in the spawned thread produces a permanent hang rather than a test failure. The FTQ-026 fix added StaleRecoveryBarrierGuard for the install/clear race, but the Barrier::wait() at line 342 remains exposed to this panic-propagation gap. Fix: replace Arc<Barrier> with a channel-based rendezvous using recv_timeout(Duration::from_secs(5)), or use std::thread::scope so panics propagate from the spawned thread, or add a watchdog channel that the spawned thread signals before blocking at the barrier." ;
  triage:category "FTQ" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-S" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-05-09T20:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
